<title>USA: U.S. new home sales slighhtly lower in September.</title>
<headline>U.S. new home sales slighhtly lower in September.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales of new homes edged lower in September from August's torrid pace as the housing market remained buoyant, according to Commerce Department figures released on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The department said sales of new homes slipped 0.5 percent in September to a seasonally adjusted annual rate of 816,000. That was just below August's revised rate of 820,000, but was still the second-highest level since April 1986.</p>
</text>
